The coating was subjected to various electrolytic conditions in order to verify durability, stability, resistance to reverse current, as well as resistance to various electrolyte impurities such as Mn, leveling agents, and other organics. Accelerated life tests were conducted according to internal De Nora test protocols (@ 1, 3, 5, 10 and 30 kA/m<sup>2</sup> ). In parallel, tests were carried out at current densities more representative of industrial Cu EW tankhouse, in a range of 300-600 A/m<sup>2</sup> . The results from the most significant tests are summarized below. 

